	(text "FDDSynthPro carrier: an Olimex RP2350-PICO2-BB48R as a 3.5-inch PC floppy drive.\nPin map: src/config.h and docs/wiring.md. Every floppy signal is active low (overbar).\n\nU1  Solder the BB48R flat or in 1x27 sockets. Its microSD slot is underneath, at the end\n    away from USB: keep that area and the space past the edge clear (courtyard).\n    GP8 (PSRAM) and GP9-11, GP24 (SD card) are the board's own: never connect them.\nU2  SN7407DR (SOIC-14), from VBUS (5 V). It pulls the cable low; the GPIOs drive its inputs.\nR1-R10  10k pull-ups (the FeatherWing host). R11-R20  1k pull-ups to PC_TERM: fit a jumper on J7\n    for a real PC (909 ohms in all). U2, C1, R1-R20 and J1 are fitted by JLCPCB (the LCSC field).\nJ2  SSD1306 OLED (or use the BB48R's own Qwiic socket: same I2C1 pins).\nJ3  Encoder: a KY-040 module plugs in as it is; a bare encoder needs only CLK, DT, SW and GND\n    (the firmware uses internal pull-ups). J4: a push button to GND.\nJ5  Adafruit MAX98357A in its own pin order; GAIN and SD left open."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 236.22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e67eea18-f833-5dfd-9c7c-6ce03e643c1c")
	)
